WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.180
Speaker 1: of the questions for like a year,
I guess, but particularly in the last three

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.889
to four months, is what is happening at the
Justice Department under the stewardship of

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:12.450
Attorney General Merrick Garland.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.279
Why is there not investigation, criminal investigation
going on of at least some of the things that

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:20.180
former President Donald Trump did?

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.890
We have now received confirmation from the
Attorney General, Merrick Garland, that the

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:31.940
Justice Department indeed received information
about the classified records found among the

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:36.410
documents recovered from Trump's Mar a Lago
and that the Justice Department is looking

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.840
into it now.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.070
This colloquially means that they are investigating.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:46.400
Whether this would technically be called an
open criminal investigation is a question

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.640
mark.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.269
NPR reporting Attorney General Merrick Garland
said the Justice Department is aware that

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:57.829
classified material has been found on Trump's
Mar a Lago property, but didn't explicitly

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:02.460
confirm a federal probe is underway.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.940
Let's take a look at the video clip.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:05.140
This is during a press conference.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.650
The audio is not great, but I think we will
be able to make out what's being said.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:10.799
Speaker 5: Questions.

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:14.900
Last week, the National Archives revealed
that it found classified information in 15

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.860
boxes of documents stored at Mar a Lago.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.439
Is the Justice Department investigating to
determine how the how that classified information

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:24.600
out there and who might have access?

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:30.759
So as as the archivist said in a letter that
was sent to the Congress, the National Archives

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:36.040
has informed the Justice Department of this
and communicated with it, and we will do what

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:37.490
we always do under these circumstances.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.940
Look at the facts and law and take it from
there.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:45.090
Speaker 1: So, you know, he's using very careful
language, he says.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:50.180
We have received the information and we are
going to do what we always do.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:54.700
We're going to look at the facts and we're
going to look at the law now.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.530
I think he's being very careful here.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:03.750
He is not saying we have opened a federal
investigation because that's very specific

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.770
and formal language.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:12.800
He is saying we are investigating and at this
point, is this merely a semantic question?

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:20.860
It may be because I see no interest whatsoever
in seriously looking at the possibility of

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.020
indicting Donald Trump.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.600
I mean, I just I just don't see it.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.960
So the fact that he's informally saying there's
an investigation without calling it a federal

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.670
probe, I think is not ultimately going to
be super meaningful.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:38.590
Now, of course, at this point, there would
be a real question for all the people who

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.980
back in 2016 said, I'm not voting for Hillary,
I'm voting for Trump because Hillary can't

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.360
be trusted with sensitive information.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:52.480
Hillary can't be trusted with classified information
or emails, the private email server, et cetera,

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.890
et cetera.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:58.830
Those people should now be saying, Wow, if
those were my concerns with Hillary, I never

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.510
should have voted for Donald Trump.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:06.620
But if you actually go and talk to them, the
vast majority will just excuse away this behavior

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.280
and say it's not really that bad or Trump
was justified in doing it, or it's a witch

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.670
hunt or the claims are untrue or whatever
the case may be.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.710
I've even seen online some conservative.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:24.340
I don't have a really conservative, some Trumpian
reactionaries saying Trump did everything

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:25.690
right here.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:31.550
Trump's own people found the classified documents
and called the National Archives and said,

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:32.650
Hey, guys, we've got this stuff.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.840
You should come and get it really quickly.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.300
There is no evidence that that's what took
place, right?

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:44.940
The narrative they want to create is Trump
had no idea about these documents, and Trump

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:49.690
staff found them and immediately of their
own volition called the National Archives

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.000
and said, Come and get the documents.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:57.541
Of course, there is no evidence that that
is the story, but at the end of the day, I

00:03:57.541 --> 00:04:03.280
don't believe Merrick Garland has any interest
in indicting a former president, and the fact

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:11.470
that they are generally investigating without
confirming an open federal probe is a distinction.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:15.890
But I don't think it will make a functional
difference in terms of what we are to expect.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:20.510
If you think Garland might have an appetite
for indicting Trump, let me know.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.660
I've seen no evidence to suggest that that's
the case.

